  "body": "Requested by mkinney (2026-11-20, \"Yes on issue for machine\"), from a Discord user (MisterMaker) who owns an Ooznest WorkBee CNC router and wants to cut 2D drawings on it.\n\nCamCraft has no WorkBee machine file; the closest is the generic `assets/machines/grblhal-3axis.mch`.\n\nTo confirm with the owner (through mkinney) before the values are final:\n- the controller: Ooznest BlackBox (grbl), a grblHAL board, or another one, and its firmware version,\n- the frame size (WorkBee 1010, 1050, 1510 or 1515, or a custom size) and the X/Y/Z travel,\n- the spindle or router (trim router with manual speed, or a VFD spindle with S words), and the max feed and rapid rates,\n- the probe or touch plate, if any, and where machine zero is.\n\nWork:\n- A `workbee-*.mch` from the public Ooznest specifications (frame sizes, travels; no other CAM product's post or machine file), using the grbl post that matches the controller.\n- Machine-picker entry and the machines README row.\n- A post conformance golden of a short 2D profile.\n\nDone means: the machine is in the picker, a 2D contour posts for it, and its values are confirmed by the owner (or marked \"from the public spec, not confirmed\" in the file).\n",
